{"type":"message","id":"823eb205","parentId":"67c4db3c","timestamp":"2026-05-31T02:06:55.583Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good, now the send_message function has proper exception handling. But I also need to check the `get_weather` function - it already has try/except, so that's fine.\n\nNow the main issue is that the scheduler process crashes and the watchdog restarts it each time. With the fix, even if the network fails, the scheduler will log the error and continue running instead of crashing.\n\nBut wait - there's another issue. The watchdog might be killing the scheduler too aggressively. Let me also check if the watchdog is properly managing the scheduler.\n\nActually, the main fix is done. The send_message function now catches exceptions and returns False instead of crashing. This means even if Feishu API is down or network is unstable, the scheduler will keep running and retry on the next loop.\n\nBut there's a subtle issue: the scheduler uses `sent_today` to avoid sending duplicate messages. If the first attempt fails (network error), the task key is still added to `sent_today`, so it won't retry. Let me check...\n\nLooking at the main loop:\n```python\nif task_key not in sent_today and abs(current_minutes - task_minutes) <= 0:\n    ...\n    send_message(msg)\n    sent_today.add(task_key)\n```\n\nThe `sent_today.add(task_key)` always runs, even if `send_message` returns False. So failed messages won't be retried! I should only add to `sent_today` on success.\n\nLet me fix that too.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"还有个问题：推送失败时也会标记「已发送」，导致不会重试。"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_bF17GimVtGe6MrpNafXA9868","name":"edit","arguments":{"old_string":"                send_message(msg)\n                sent_today.add(task_key)","new_string":"                if send_message(msg):\n                    sent_today.add(task_key)\n","path":"/root/.openclaw/workspace/scripts/reminder_scheduler.py"}