{"type":"message","id":"2c268272","parentId":"489f5ef8","timestamp":"2026-05-31T02:07:12.491Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The scheduler is running (PID 20095). The watchdog might have restarted it already with the new code, or the old process wasn't actually killed. Let me check when it was started and confirm the fix is in place by checking the log.\n\nActually, the issue is that I can't kill the process because it's being auto-restarted by the watchdog somehow. Let me just check the log to see if the fix is working.\n\nActually, let me think about this differently. The key fix is:\n1. Exception handling in send_message and get_token\n2. Only mark as sent on success\n\nThe scheduler process (PID 20095) was started at 10:04:54 today (from the log). This is the current instance. Since I edited the Python file, the process needs to be restarted to pick up the new code.\n\nThe watchdog checks the scheduler and restarts it if not running. So I need to kill the scheduler, then the watchdog will restart it with the updated code.\n\nBut pkill keeps getting SIGTERM'd. Let me try using `kill` directly on the PID.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_C5znKyKIi1FbGsKZyrTS8334","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"kill 20095 2>/dev/null; sleep 5; pgrep -f reminder_scheduler.py; echo \"---\"; cat /root/.openclaw/logs/scheduler.log | tail -5","timeout":12}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":98,"output":558,"cacheRead":31104,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":31760,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780193226141}}
